        "text": "Some ions are made of several atoms bonded together, with an overall charge. These are called polyatomic ions. Hydroxide and nitrate each have a charge of minus one. Carbonate and sulfate are minus two. Phosphate is minus three. And ammonium is the positive one, plus one. Each stays together as a single unit, so you treat it just like one ion. You'll need to learn these six by heart."
